Description: Activate the window opened for the launch, not a restored one, with the launch activation token on Wayland.
 GTK 3 reads the activation token Firefox is launched with from DESKTOP_STARTUP_ID and activates the first toplevel
 it maps with it. During startup session restore that is the first restored window shown. mutter does not activate
 it and marks it as demanding attention instead, and the window opened for the launch, holding the URL or the start
 page, stays without the token.
 .
 The token is now removed from GTK at startup and given to nsGTKToolkit, whose token the first window shown uses,
 as it already does for a launch passed to a running Firefox. While session restore runs, a window which the
 compositor places from the session, restored under its saved ID, does not use it. A window opened for the launch
 is shown when session restore finishes (wayland-session-restore-show-waiting-windows.patch) and uses it then. A
 token which no window used, because every window was restored, is dropped at that point, so that a window opened
 later transfers the focus to itself as usual.
Author: Mitar
Bug: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2090734
Forwarded: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340739
